plan.prompt:
Read-only research plan for: ${question}
Optional evidence context: ${context}
Parts are ONLY the material parts of the user's question (ids p1..pN in order); extra evidence angles are tasks, not parts. Decompose into 1–6 distinct, verifiable tasks; each task lists the partIds it serves; every part needs at least one task. Do not use overlapping summaries of the same docs. Prioritize the central product/scope question before ancillary setup, version pins or citation polish. For claims about whether a UI exists, inspect actual routes, assets or official product boundaries rather than relying on README silence; absence of evidence is not disproof. Choose local for repository evidence, github for external GitHub evidence, web for public sources. Treat context and search snippets only as leads; open sources before treating claims as facts. If a source cannot be opened, make verification a task, not a fact. No writing or delegation. Return only structured JSON {parts:[{id,question}],tasks:[{source,question,purpose,partIds}]} where purpose names the question part and distinct evidence to check.

work.prompt:
Question: ${question}
Atomic task: ${item}
Read only. Open sources rather than trusting snippets, prior context or other agents. Return individual one-fact claims with short verbatim excerpt, reference (local path/line or opened URL), and source identity. Do not invent citations. If inaccessible or contested, report a gap; distinguish absence of evidence from disproof. Return only structured JSON {claims:[{claim,excerpt,reference,source}],gaps:[string]}.

evaluator.prompt:
Read-only evaluation. Original question: ${question}
Plan: ${plan}
All accumulated rounds, all-settled results, failures and unresolved gaps: ${feedback}
Check coverage of each plan part, especially the central product/scope question. Independently open primary sources yourself for selected disputed, consequential or weak claims at local file paths and web/GitHub URLs; worker excerpts, snippets and schema validity do not prove facts. For a material actionable gap (such as an omitted upstream README fetch or missing API/CLI source), choose a distinct accessible source-opening task; if a source fetch failed, try a different access method where available. For UI existence, inspect routes, assets or official product boundaries; prioritize this over citation polish or commit pins. Do not count two views of one source as independent. Follow leads only to close named gaps, never to expand scope or repeat the same search. Return decision:'continue' with a linked task when a useful accessible check can resolve a material gap. Return decision:'sufficient', tasks:[] with gaps only when no useful accessible check remains; immaterial or inaccessible gaps do not force continuation. If all plan parts are supported, return decision:'sufficient', gaps:[], tasks:[]. Never stop because a round or task bound is reached; the runtime handles bounds. Record inaccessible or contested evidence as gaps. Return only {decision:'sufficient'|'continue',gaps:[{id,description}],tasks:[{gapId,item:{source,question,purpose,partIds}}]}.

synthesize.prompt:
Produce a read-only cited Markdown research report and structured findings. Question: ${question}
Context (unverified leads): ${context}
Plan: ${plan}
Complete terminal research result, including every round and all-settled failures: ${research}
Use only validated structured claims with opened source excerpts/provenance for factual claims; reopen cited local files and web/GitHub sources where needed, never trust worker excerpts or search snippets as independently verified. Mark single-source, disputed and independently checked findings separately (verification: independently-checked, single-source, or disputed). Independent checks are agent judgment, not a schema truth proof. Include citation keys in Markdown and accepted findings, sources and limitations. Reject unsupported claims; preserve every failure, unverified gap and contested finding even when bounded feedback says sufficient. Report verifiedCoverage exactly once per plan part id. A material failure, unresolved material gap, or disputed finding downgrades its part to partial or missing; immaterial or recovered failures and gaps stay reported without downgrading. Outcome follows coverage: succeeded when every part is supported (omit reason); partial when useful findings remain but a part is partial or missing (reason names unresolved parts); failed when no reliable findings remain. Return structured JSON only; never write an output file (runtime handles oversized result artifacts).
